id: pm-bqyk1z
title: "Public SDK class members and exported type declarations still name package types their entrypoint does not export (98 class-member and 875 type-declaration references), beyond the function signatures pm-gh1667 gated"
description: "Found while fixing pm-gh1667 on 2026.11.7. The sdk-surface-snapshot generator now refuses an entrypoint whose exported function signatures name a package type the entrypoint does not export (signature_type_reachability), and the 281 function-signature gaps were closed. The same forgotten-export rule still fails on two wider scopes, measured on the emitted declarations: (1) public class members: 98 gaps, 83 distinct types, almost all PmClient methods exported from ./sdk/core (for example CommitItemMutationsOptions, ItemTransactionStatus, StatsResult, PmClientRunArgs), which ./sdk exports but ./sdk/core does not; (2) members of exported interfaces and type aliases: 875 gaps, 463 distinct types across every entrypoint (./sdk 185, ./sdk/runtime 243, ./sdk/core 133, ./sdk/testing 90). A consumer can call PmClient.commitItemMutations from ./sdk/core but cannot name its options type from that entrypoint. Extending the gate is the same analysis applied to class member signatures and to the transitive closure of exported declarations; the closure is large enough that it needs a deliberate per-entrypoint policy (re-export, or declare an entrypoint as a narrow view that points at ./sdk for named types) rather than a blind re-export. Duplicate check: searched forgotten export, unexported type, public type names, class members and PmClient types across all statuses; pm-obbh43 and pm-suhxny cover value exports only."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: api-surface,extensions,sdk,types
created_at: "2026-11-07T08:59:59.177Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T10:39:46.737Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The SDK surface gate checks public class member signatures and refuses a member that names an unexported package type, or records the entrypoint as a declared narrow view that names its canonical entrypoint; Every gap is closed or covered by a declared narrow-view policy, with the count recorded in the snapshot; A negative control that removes one class-member re-export fails the gate; A decision is recorded for the transitive type-declaration closure: gate it, or bound it with a measured ratchet"
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: medium
severity: low
repro_steps: "In a NodeNext strict consumer: import type { CommitItemMutationsOptions } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/core' fails with TS2305, although PmClient from sdk/core takes it"
expected_result: Types named by public class members are importable from the entrypoint that exports the class
actual_result: 98 class-member and 875 type-declaration references name types their entrypoint does not export
affected_version: 2026.11.7
component: sdk
