comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T10:39:46.737Z","harness:claude-code","Scope evidence from the pm-gh1665/1666/1667 batch review (Codex round 4, 2026-11-07): the function-and-value signature gate in scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs stops at a named annotation. When an internal module declares type Runner = (options: Hidden) => void and const run: Runner, and an entrypoint re-exports run and Runner but not Hidden, the gate reports missing: [] because Runner itself is exported; the same holds for callable interfaces. That is the transitive type-declaration closure this item owns (the 875 type-declaration references measured above), not a function-signature gap, so it was deferred here rather than fixed in the batch. The fix belongs with the closure policy: when an exported type alias or interface is reached from a public value, walk its declaration (or the checker's resolved call signatures) and apply the same reachability rule, with the per-entrypoint narrow-view decision recorded in the AC.\n"
body: ""
